title: Route sibling XCM over speculative messaging
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    To enable this transport, place `SpecMsgRouter` before `XcmpQueue`. HRMP keeps priority
    until the runtime marks the channel as closing. With HRMP closed or marked as closing,
    an open speculative messaging channel can carry the XCM. If that channel closes during
    cutover, new sends fail until it reopens or the runtime clears the HRMP closing flag.
    Wait for the sender and relay queues to drain before requesting HRMP closure.

    Handle `AggregateMessageOrigin::SpecMsg(InChannelId)` in exhaustive matches on the
    Cumulus and bridge-hub queue origins. Each inbound channel has its own queue and
    executes XCM with the sender's sibling origin. Runtimes using the messaging pallet must
    configure `ChannelManagementOrigin` for HRMP cutover and inbound queue pause or resume.

    Offboarding cleanup clears queue pauses for the listed lanes so previously queued XCM can drain.

    EnqueueToXcmQueue accepts only the XCM lane (domain 0, channel 0).

    For sibling XCM benchmarks over spec-msg, use the messaging pallet as the
    `ToParachainDeliveryHelper` setup type and the router's `Price` as `PriceForDelivery`.
    Leave HRMP closed for the benchmark destination.
crates:
- name: cumulus-pallet-spec-messaging
  bump: major
- name: cumulus-primitives-core
  bump: major
- name: parachains-common
  bump: major
- name: bridge-hub-common
  bump: major
